Here `task` arrives as a method parameter from callers like `verifyAndRepairWorkflowTasks`, which simply does `workflow.getTasks().forEach(this::verifyAndRepairTask);` without any prior status normalization. Since `TaskModel.status` is nullable and can be left unset by upstream components, at the time `verifyAndRepairTask` is called, `task.status` may legitimately be null.

When the JVM evaluates the condition:

```java
